3. StructuredGaussianMixtures.jl (Exp4 dependency)
--------------------------------------------------

Experiment 4 uses sisl/StructuredGaussianMixtures.jl:

https://github.com/sisl/StructuredGaussianMixtures.jl

The upstream project is MIT licensed, Copyright (c) 2025 Arec Jamgochian
<arec.jamgochian@terraai.earth> and contributors. It is not redistributed in
this repository. `paper/envs/idm` fetches it as a Git dependency from the fork

https://github.com/lea-m-hadzic/StructuredGaussianMixtures.jl

pinned to

  commit  `182b322e8f58b54c28c8bebf60466c047839c6af`
          (also reachable as branch `aris-exp4-b15` and tag `aris-jmlr-exp4`)
  tree    `00e19319a721e9c900648e69faf41199b2b85541`

This commit is upstream commit `aef6158313edccd91082039086aaa5b3b1674f8c`
plus one local commit, modifying:

  `src/fit.jl`
      Adds numerical floors to the diagonal variance in the FactorEM inner
      M-step:
      `Dinv = 1 ./ max.(D, 1e-8)`
      `D .= max.(D, 1e-4)`

  `src/predict.jl`
      Adds a numerical floor to the input-block diagonal variance in the LRD
      conditional prediction path:
      `1 ./ sqrt.(max.(D₁, 1e-8))`

Experiment 4 depends on these numerical-stability changes for its
150-dimensional MAP-EM fit. `paper/envs/idm/Manifest.toml` pins the fork by
URL, exact commit (`repo-rev`), and Git tree hash (`git-tree-sha1`), so this
commit is used instead of the registry version and Pkg verifies the fetched
source.

The package `Project.toml` at this commit retains the upstream version string
`0.1.0`, although its contents differ from the registered v0.1.0. The
`StructuredGaussianMixtures` version `0.1.0` recorded in
`paper/results/exp4/meta.json` refers to this commit.

Earlier revisions of this repository vendored the same source under
`third_party/StructuredGaussianMixtures/`. That copy was used to produce the
Exp4 results; its code files are identical to the pinned commit.


